{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793441023,"nonce":"uiWGGlEr+xEw8Sf+WaKrmsK5PB4=","message":"Direction: parity with web standards, no Blinc dialect. Only flow shaders and pointer query are domain extras.\n\nDone in 8fa75b12 and b7252d2e:\n- `transition` follows CSS: longhands take comma lists in any order, no property means `all`, `background-color`/`border-top-color`/`padding-left`/`translate`/`inset`/`outline` cover what they animate, last matching entry wins, each property keeps its own duration/delay/easing (one lane per timing), a running transition survives a change to other properties.\n- Colours interpolate premultiplied.\n- `:active` matches the pressed element's ancestors.\n- A component-layer rule gives way to a fluent value (component half of the precedence flip).\n- Button hover/press/disabled looks are `:hover`/`:active`/`:disabled` rules with `transition`: cn in CN_STYLES, layout in `ua_styles::UA_STYLES` (registered by the runners). The bound-colour engine (`Div::transition`) is removed. The cn button state golden matched the old record apart from the press scale and a hovered-and-pressed button keeping its hover colour (both web behaviour).\n\nStill open:\n- Other cn components compute state colours in Rust: Switch, Checkbox, Radio, Input, Select, DropdownMenu trigger, Toggle, Badge. Each moves to rules the same way.\n- App rules still beat fluent values (the other half of the flip, see 7cabafe).\n- Not animatable yet: font-weight, letter-spacing, line-height, per-side border widths, grid tracks. No `steps()`/`step-end` timing, no `transition-behavior`.\n- A component-layer state rule applies after an app base rule, so layer order does not hold across the base/state phases; cn avoids it with `:not(:disabled)`.\n- Not observed in a running window or wasm.","files":null}]}